</math> potatoes and saved&nbsp;<math alttext="10 percent sign"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of them to plant next year. How many of the harvested potatoes did Isabel save to plant next year?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3bee3533-7274-41e0-8e2e-a0ca51fe8cb0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"66\"><mn>66</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d5c3badd-6269-4bb7-94bd-ab11eb77b9d3","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"76\"><mn>76</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5592e014-97dc-48fb-8dad-642cb6af912d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f50ab268-0d3d-4174-abd4-ba1fa42e9c92","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"86\"><mn>86</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d5c3badd-6269-4bb7-94bd-ab11eb77b9d3"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The number of harvested potatoes Isabel saved to plant next year can be calculated by multiplying the total number of potatoes Isabel harvested, <math alttext="760"><mn>760</mn>
</math>, by the proportion of potatoes she saved. Since she saved&nbsp;<math alttext="10 percent sign"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the potatoes she harvested, the proportion of potatoes she saved is&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction 10 Over 100 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="0.1"><mn>0.1</mn>
</math>. Multiplying <math alttext="760"><mn>760</mn>
</math> by this proportion gives <math alttext="760 left parenthesis 0.1 right parenthesis"><mn>760</mn><mfenced><mn>0.1</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="76"><mn>76</mn>
</math>, potatoes that she saved to plant next year.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"273b7f37","external_id":"691ec468-2184-424c-ac94-53b3d07a4270","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"6f9672bd-b7cd-4f7e-8f90-987e2a562f64","uId":"a88b0fef-4b0b-4412-b62e-7866616be3da","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Isabel grows potatoes in her garden. This year, she harvested <math alttext=\"760\"><mn>760</mn>\n</math> potatoes and saved&nbsp;<math alttext=\"10 percent sign\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of them to plant next year. How many of the harvested potatoes did Isabel save to plant next year?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3bee3533-7274-41e0-8e2e-a0ca51fe8cb0","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"66\"><mn>66</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d5c3badd-6269-4bb7-94bd-ab11eb77b9d3","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"76\"><mn>76</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5592e014-97dc-48fb-8dad-642cb6af912d","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f50ab268-0d3d-4174-abd4-ba1fa42e9c92","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"86\"><mn>86</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["d5c3badd-6269-4bb7-94bd-ab11eb77b9d3"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. The number of harvested potatoes Isabel saved to plant next year can be calculated by multiplying the total number of potatoes Isabel harvested, <math alttext=\"760\"><mn>760</mn>\n</math>, by the proportion of potatoes she saved. Since she saved&nbsp;<math alttext=\"10 percent sign\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the p