</math> marbles remained in the group. How many marbles were removed from the group?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"f2cd0457-13d2-4ec9-b718-33f83b65737f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"60ad70f0-a97d-4aa3-876f-1f2f17c4a847","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c0999fec-9188-4509-9c78-160248d99c24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"450\"><mn>450</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a5d0ed85-963f-4d95-bb10-8ccaa5c9ec43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,800\"><mn>1,800</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["60ad70f0-a97d-4aa3-876f-1f2f17c4a847"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. It's given that <math alttext="20 percent sign"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the original number of marbles were removed from the group. Let <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represent the original number of marbles in the group. It follows that <math alttext="StartFraction 20 Over 100 EndFraction x"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>, or <math alttext="0.20 x"><mn>0.20</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, marbles were removed from the group. Therefore, <math alttext="x minus 0.20 x"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mi>x</mi></math> marbles remained in the group. It's also given that <math alttext="360"><mn>360</mn>
</math> marbles remained in the group. Thus, <math alttext="x minus 0.20 x equals 360"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></math>, or <math alttext="0.80 x equals 360"><mn>0.80</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="0.80"><mn>0.80</mn></math> yields <math alttext="x equals 450"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>450</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="450"><mn>450</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> in the expression <math alttext="0.20 x"><mn>0.20</mn><mi>x</mi></math> yields <math alttext="0.20 left parenthesis 450 right parenthesis"><mn>0.20</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>450</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math>. Therefore, <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math> marbles were removed from the group.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is <math alttext="20 percent sign"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the remaining number of marbles.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the original number of marbles, not the number of marbles that were removed.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"2afd3cec","external_id":"9aa8fbdb-6e32-4b91-81d7-831d0518641e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"bb89ef6a-ee00-4591-b5ed-ad0dd5ffd276","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">After <math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the original number of marbles in a group were removed from the group, <math alttext=\"360\"><mn>360</mn>\n</math> marbles remained in the group. How many marbles were removed from the group?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"f2cd0457-13d2-4ec9-b718-33f83b65737f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"60ad70f0-a97d-4aa3-876f-1f2f17c4a847","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"c0999fec-9188-4509-9c78-160248d99c24","content":"<p><math alttext=\"450\"><mn>450</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a5d0ed85-963f-4d95-bb10-8ccaa5c9ec43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,800\"><mn>1,800</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["60ad70f0-a97d-4aa3-876f-1f2f17c4a847"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that <math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the original number of marbles were removed from the group. Let <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> represent the original number of marbles in the group. It follows that <math alttext=\"StartFraction 20 Over 100 EndFraction x\"><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"0.20 x\"><mn>0.20</mn><mi>x</mi></math>, marbles were removed from the group. Therefore, <math alttext=\"x minus 0