3fbc9a\">12</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-16abc0e7-eab5-48e4-a118-16c089fd1d71\">160</td>\n                    </tr>\n                    <tr>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-d71d147b-cd08-49be-8317-738eddd0424a\">Total</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-9ed36616-f4e1-449a-a5a8-dc845783194d\">50</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-9365ff2f-d6cf-470b-8096-75159d6dd1a4\">157</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-bd4212bb-c679-4c9e-863d-23f26a52d035\">223</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-7dd0ab79-08db-4bf9-81d8-917930011cfd\">70</td>\n                      <td class=\"tcp-9a56db65-2519-4d4a-a079-c77961aec943\">500</td>\n                    </tr>\n                  </tbody>\n                </table>\n                <p></p>\n              <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A supervisor at a call center reviewed 500 calls taken by four employees and rated the employees&rsquo; performance on each call on a scale from 1 star to 4 stars. The ratings for each employee are shown in the table above. According to the table, to the nearest whole percent, what percent of Employee A&rsquo;s calls received a rating of 1 star?</p></div>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3%</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">11%</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">16%</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">32%</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The percent of Employee A&rsquo;s calls that received a rating of 1 star is the number of&nbsp;Employee A&rsquo;s 1-star calls divided by the total number of Employee A&rsquo;s&nbsp;calls. This quotient,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"16 over 145\"></span>,&nbsp;is approximately equal to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 1 1 0 3\"></span>, or&nbsp;<span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"11 point 0 3 percent\"></span>. To the nearest whole percent, this is 11%.<br><br>\nChoice A is incorrect. This is the percent of all calls taken by Employee A that received a rating of 1 star. Choice C is incorrect and may result from a conceptual error. For example, 16 is the number, not the percent, of calls taken by Employee A that received a rating of 1 star. Choice D is incorrect. This is the percent of all calls that received a rating of 1 star that were taken by Employee A.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959635,"updateDate":1691007959635}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959635, 1691007959635),
    ($SATQ$2df8f293$SATQ$, $SATQ$b38bd503-bc4e-485d-a578-38da101ab31a$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Each vertex of a <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math>-sided polygon is labeled with one of the <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math> letters <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> through <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi>
</math>, with a different letter at each vertex. If one vertex is selected at random, what is the probability that the letter <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math> will be at the selected vertex? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$[".0714","1/14"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$[".0714","1/14"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="one fourteenth"><mfrac>
<mn>1</mn>
<mn>14</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>. If one vertex of the polygon is selected at random, the probability that the letter <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math> will be at the selected vertex is equal to the number of vertices labeled with the letter <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math> divided by the total number of vertices. It's given that each vertex is labeled with one of the <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math> letters <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math> through <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi>
</math>, with a different letter at each vertex. It follows that there is <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> vertex labeled with the letter <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math>. It's also given that the polygon is <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math>-sided. It follows that there are a total of <math alttext="14"><mn>14</mn>
</math> vertices. Thus, the probability that the letter <math alttext="upper D"><mi>D</mi>
</math> will be at the selected vertex is <math alttext="one fourteenth"><mfrac>
<mn>1</mn>
<mn>14</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>. Note that 1/14, .0714, and 0.071 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"2df8f293","external_id":"b38bd503-bc4e-485d-a578-38da101ab31a","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4af89aa1-f7eb-4094-bc0a-a8eb37dfb0b8","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each vertex of a <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>-sided polygon is labeled with one of the <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> letters <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> through <math alttext=\"upper N\"><mi>N</mi>\n</math>, with a different letter at each vertex. If one vertex is selected at random, what is the probability that the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math> will be at the selected vertex? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)</p>","answerOptions":null,"keys":[".0714","1/14"],"correct_answer":[".0714","1/14"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"one fourteenth\"><mfrac>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. If one vertex of the polygon is selected at random, the probability that the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math> will be at the selected vertex is equal to the number of vertices labeled with the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math> divided by the total number of vertices. It's given that each vertex is labeled with one of the <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> letters <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> through <math alttext=\"upper N\"><mi>N</mi>\n</math>, with a different letter at each vertex. It follows that there is <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> vertex labeled with the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math>. It's also given that the polygon is <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>-sided. It follows that there are a total of <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> vertices. Thus, the probability that the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math> will be at the selected vertex is <math alttext=\"one fourteenth\"><mfrac>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. Note that 1/14, .0714, and 0.071 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959835,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"2df8f293","skill_cd":"Q.E.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","createDate":1691007959835,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":null,"external_id":"b38bd503-bc4e-485d-a578-38da101ab31a","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"4af89aa1-f7eb-4094-bc0a-a8eb37dfb0b8","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"spr","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each vertex of a <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math>-sided polygon is labeled with one of the <math alttext=\"14\"><mn>14</mn>\n</math> letters <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math> through <math alttext=\"upper N\"><mi>N</mi>\n</math>, with a different letter at each vertex. If one vertex is selected at random, what is the probability that the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\"><mi>D</mi>\n</math> will be at the selected vertex? (Express your answer as a decimal or fraction, not as a percent.)</p>","keys":[".0714","1/14"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"one fourteenth\"><mfrac>\n<mn>1</mn>\n<mn>14</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. If one vertex of the polygon is selected at random, the probability that the letter <math alttext=\"upper D\