<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>The scatterplot has 10 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending down from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:</li>
<li>The line of best fit slants down from left to right.<br>
<ul>
<li>5 points are touching the line of best fit.</li>
<li>2 points are above the line of best fit.</li>
<li>3 points are below the line of best fit.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(1 comma 7)</li>
<li>(4 comma 5)</li>
<li>(10 comma 1)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Which of the following is closest to the slope of this line of best fit?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"86888108-edc9-4270-86f0-e1bbc0d00236","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0e15860b-f62b-41e2-be39-3fa60fe81fc9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.7\"><mn>0.7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"78a2b65b-61c5-47e0-b6db-4a82722918f6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 0.7\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d49bb74a-8575-4a6b-90d8-6a9ff347d7a4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 7\"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["78a2b65b-61c5-47e0-b6db-4a82722918f6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. A line of best fit is shown in the scatterplot such that as the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> increases, the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> decreases. It follows that the slope of the line of best fit shown is negative. The slope of a line in the <em>xy</em>-plane that passes through the points <math alttext="left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext="left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> can be calculated as <math alttext="StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. The line of best fit shown passes approximately through the points <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext="left parenthesis 10 comma 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Substituting <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> for <math alttext="left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext="left parenthesis 10 comma 1 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> for <math alttext="left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> in&nbsp;<math alttext="StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> yields the slope of the line being approximately <math alttext="StartFraction 1 minus 8 Over 10 minus 0 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="StartFraction negative 7 Over 10 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext="negative 0.7"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn></math>. Therefore, of the given choices, <math alttext="negative 0.7"><mo>-</mo><mn>0.7</mn></math> is the closest to the slope of this line of best fit.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The line of best fit shown has a negative slope, not a positive slope.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The line of best fit shown has a negative slope, not a positive slope.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"2e74e403","external_id":"57cffc23-e07d-4acc-9f42-b8eacfd50cd8","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"887f1aa1-20b3-485d-b028-e6f908d9e3b6","uId":"283dbc1e-12d1-426d-a74f-8481d22d767c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given scatterplot, a line of best fit for the data is shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 10 in increments of 1. The y axis ranges from 0 to 10 in increments of 1. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.200821 268.02 \nL 271.689179 268.02 \nL 271.689179 7.2 \nL 9.200821 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xti