</math> to <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"312ba47c","external_id":"d88daa3d-713d-4905-8fc3-540215e519e9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"c284b25b-900d-4797-8bda-9db7773107c5","uId":"1987da32-b3cc-4447-8cd0-66753b708611","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In a box of pens, the ratio of black pens to red pens is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. There are <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> black pens in the box. How many red pens are in the box?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"dd88b5f3-bd71-440b-a1d7-26abace64716","content":"<p><math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"573e0c27-695e-4826-849b-df308c77f32a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1e450f5c-4abe-47b3-8301-3f327175bc5f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"aceaba98-818d-4259-9f9a-1f35215e9147","content":"<p><math alttext=\"320\"><mn>320</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["dd88b5f3-bd71-440b-a1d7-26abace64716"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the ratio of black pens to red pens is <math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, there are <math alttext=\"one eighth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> as many red pens as black pens in the box. It&rsquo;s also given that there are <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> black pens in the box. Therefore, the number of red pens is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"one eighth\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> of the <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</m